# Every text file is checked out with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# A Windows checkout has CRLF by default, and three of the shell's tests
# read their own source (`include_str!`) and match it literally — so the
# line endings become part of what they assert, and the tests fail on a
# checkout whose lines end differently, for a reason that has nothing to
# do with the code. The same endings are what the shell's own scripts
# expect when they run under a Windows Git Bash.
#
# Nothing is renormalised: every text file in the index is already LF, so
# this changes the working tree only.
* text=auto eol=lf
